<DocsPageSubtitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSubtitle>

<Heading Size="HeadingSize.Is3">
    Control the Exposed Schema
</Heading>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Define an explicit schema for user-facing editors so only intended properties, labels, order, and editor types are exposed. Group related properties and use domain language instead of showing implementation-oriented member names. Secrets, internal identifiers, and security-sensitive settings should never be included through automatic discovery.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<Heading Size="HeadingSize.Is3">
    Validate User-Facing Edits
</Heading>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Validate a change before applying it to the source object and show feedback next to the property that needs attention. When several values are interdependent, validate the complete edited object as well as each individual field.
</DocsPageParagraph>

